---
title: "HCML Monitoring Portal: what the rebuild script does"
---
flowchart TD
    %% deploy/rebuild.sh, in the order it runs. Start with the dry-run option: it prints every command and runs none.
    %% A folder with no git is built too (labelled unknown, no live tag). The script never marks last-good itself: that is the separate --mark-good run.

    A["rebuild.sh"] --> B{"A git checkout?"}
    B -->|"no: the build is labelled unknown,<br/>and no live tag is made"| C
    B -->|"yes"| B2{"A clean tree?"}
    B2 -->|"changed files and<br/>no allow-dirty option"| X["Stop"]
    B2 -->|"clean, or dirty allowed:<br/>the build is labelled dirty"| C["Gate: parity check<br/>when both copies are there"]
    C --> D["Gate: npm run verify<br/>unless skipped"]
    D --> E["Gate: docker can read<br/>each copy's settings"]
    E --> S["For each copy, the hosted one first:<br/>save its logs"]
    S --> F["Tag the images being replaced<br/>rollback-day-month"]
    F --> G["docker compose up -d --build<br/>with the commit and the time"]
    G -->|"compose up fails"| K
    G --> H["Wait for both containers<br/>to be healthy, up to 180 s"]
    H --> I["Ask as an anonymous caller<br/>health 200, meters 401,<br/>/.env 404, /.git/config 404,<br/>a Content-Security-Policy"]
    I -->|"any failure"| K["Stop before the next copy is touched.<br/>Print the rollback steps,<br/>last-good first, and exit 1"]
    I -->|"all ok, and a copy is left"| S
    I -->|"all ok, the last copy"| J["On a clean git tree: make the<br/>local tag live-date, never pushed"]
    J --> L["Print the signed-in check<br/>that only a person can run"]
    L --> M["Later, by hand, once that check passes:<br/>rebuild.sh --mark-good keeps the images<br/>that run as last-good"]
